	"summary": {
		"text": "From Arochukwu, the Aro built a trading network across south-eastern Nigeria, backed by the prestige of their oracle, Ibini Ukpabi (the \"Long Juju\"), and by allied fighters from Abam, Ohafia and Edda. Aro settlements and fairs channelled trade, much of it in enslaved people, to Bonny and Calabar. Britain destroyed the oracle in the Anglo-Aro war of 1901–1902.",
